      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument this morning in Case Number 23-1039, Ames versus the Ohio Department of Youth Services."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Xiao Wang",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca34420a7c2cfc9b1a3c3a5e046cd01f9c3788a383d5896321cc1a9a757999a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca34420a7c2c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Based on these facts, the Sixth Circuit held that Ms. Ames had satisfied the usual requirements for stating a -- for stating a prima facie case of discrimination under Title VII, but she could not proceed because of the background circumstances rule, which the Sixth Circuit described as an additional showing unique to majority-group plaintiffs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Xiao Wang",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca34420a7c2cfc9b1a3c3a5e046cd01f9c3788a383d5896321cc1a9a757999a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca34420a7c2c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The narrow question before the Court today is whether this judge-made rule is consistent with Title VII. And we submit that it is not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1039",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca34420a7c2cfc9b1a3c3a5e046cd01f9c3788a383d5896321cc1a9a757999a5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca34420a7c2c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
